      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Blanch the pork belly pieces in boiling water for 3 minutes. Drain and pat dry."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a Dutch oven, heat the sugar over medium heat without stirring until it melts and turns a deep amber colour."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the pork pieces carefully . the caramel will spit. Toss to coat. Stir until the caramel has melted back into the pork."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the garlic, shallots, and ginger. Stir for 1 minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in the coconut water and fish sauce. Bring to the boil, then reduce to the lowest simmer. Cook uncovered for 60 to 75 minutes until the pork is very tender and the sauce has thickened."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Taste the sauce and adjust with more fish sauce if needed. It should be sweet, salty, and rich."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Garnish with spring onion. Serve with steamed jasmine rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The sauce is too sweet.",
              "cause": "The coconut water was sweetened, or too much sugar was used in the caramel.",
              "fix": "Use unsweetened coconut water. Add more fish sauce to balance the sweetness. A small squeeze of lime also helps."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The sauce evaporates completely before the pork is tender.",
              "cause": "The heat was too high.",
              "fix": "Add 100 ml of water and reduce the heat further. The braise should be at the gentlest possible simmer."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The pork skin is rubbery instead of silky.",
              "cause": "The braise was not long enough.",
              "fix": "Cook for the full 75 minutes. Pork skin needs sustained low heat to break down the collagen and become silky."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thịt heo kho dừa is a southern Vietnamese speciality from the Mekong Delta. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The delta grows coconuts in abundance and they appear in both savoury and sweet cooking throughout the region. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This dish is a variation of the national favourite thịt kho, made richer and sweeter with coconut water. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is a regular family meal and is also made in large quantities for celebrations. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Southern Vietnamese cooking is known for being sweeter than the north, and this dish shows that character clearly."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
